\title{The interpreter of the integration branch has to take up the review changes}
\taxon{Problem}
\date{2026-11-23}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{schrodingerzy}
\tag{ir}
\tag{integration}
\meta{status}{open}
\meta{created}{2026-11-23}
\import{base-macros}

\p{\strong{Status:} open.}
\p{The branch of \pr{13} changes \code{\verb~|LibcMath/IR/Interp.lean~} from the definition of \code{\verb~|Instr.exec~} to the end, for flags of instructions and for executions that go wrong, and leaves the part before it as in \pr{2}. The review of \pr{2} therefore changed only that first part and added files. What remains for the merge:}
\ul{
\li{\code{\verb~|LibcMath/IR/InterpLemmas.lean~} on that branch declares \code{\verb~|Val.toModel?_ofModel~}, which \code{\verb~|LibcMath/SpecLemmas.lean~} already has. Delete the copy.}
\li{\code{\verb~|LibcMath/IR/InterpDiag.lean~} follows \code{\verb~|Func.execFrom~}. If the interpreter there gains a way to give up that the diagnostic does not follow, \code{\verb~|Func.explain~} says so in its answer; extend \code{\verb~|explainFrom~} then. The examples in \code{\verb~|LibcMath/IR/InterpExamples.lean~} will show whether the messages changed.}
\li{The cases of \code{\verb~|Instr.exec_sound~} repeat one pattern for uniqueness, about fifteen times. \code{\verb~|grind~} closes it in the case that was tried ([ins-AJCO](ins-AJCO)). Apply it to the version of that branch, where the proofs are final, and measure the time of the file before and after: it took about four seconds before.}
}
